---
import EditorialArticle from "../../components/EditorialArticle.astro";
import { enabledPageCatalog } from "../../core/site-data";
import { buildBuildsRouteRecord } from "../../core/optional-routes";

const page = buildBuildsRouteRecord(enabledPageCatalog);
---

<EditorialArticle page={page} sectionLabel="Build decision hub">
  <p class="decision-lede">A useful build is a direction tied to a goal. Start with the activity you want to improve, then judge reliability, gear dependence, and the cost of changing course.</p>

  <div class="decision-grid">
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Goal 01</p>
      <h2>Reliable progression</h2>
      <p>Favor consistency and a setup you can keep operating while you test one change at a time.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Goal 02</p>
      <h2>Focused farming</h2>
      <p>Judge the build by repeatable clears, useful gear outcomes, and the effort required to maintain the run.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow">Goal 03</p>
      <h2>Market-aware progress</h2>
      <p>Keep progression opportunity cost visible before selling an eligible item that may be difficult to replace.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2>A short build review</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Name the activity this build should improve.</li>
    <li>Identify which gear decisions the direction depends on.</li>
    <li>Keep a stable setup while testing a new choice.</li>
    <li>Re-evaluate after a meaningful equipment or progression change.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>This Phase 2A hub does not publish class tiers, universal winners, or numeric optimization claims. Those require verified mechanics and comparable performance evidence.</p>

  <p><a class="button button--primary" href="/guides/farming/">Apply the goal to farming <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  <p>New to the decision loop? Start with the <a href="/guides/beginner-guide/">Beginner Guide</a>. Considering a sale? Read the <a href="/market/">Steam Market Guide</a>.</p>
</EditorialArticle>
